            <ArticleTitle>[Cerebral and spinal angiography with metrizamide (amipaque) (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>559-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Metrizamide (Amipaque) has been used as the contrast medium for angiography in neuroradiological investigations. Solutions containing 280 mgI/ml. are well tolerated and produce good contrast. The most important difference from previously used contrast media is the lack of pain when injections are made selectively or super-selectively into the external carotid artery and its branches, or into the spinal arteries.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
